MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima feels like a natural next choice after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's atmosphere and complex rhythms.",
    "Master of Puppets matches my interest in heavy music with intricate riffs; Ride the Lightning and The Sound of Perseverance also connect with that interest, even though I would choose Master of Puppets first."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger's raw, abrasive sound and Antichrist Superstar's industrial edge miss the melodic, rhythmically engaging heaviness I want right now.",
    "Fallen's melodic rock and Source Tags & Codes' art-rock direction each overlap with parts of my listening, but neither offers the intricate, riff-driven metal drawing me in today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The suggestions seem to treat heaviness or aggression alone as enough to interest me, although the way the riffs and rhythms develop matters more.",
    "My broader rock listening seems to carry too much weight when my latest choices make Tool and more intricate heavy music especially appealing."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent listen to 10.000 Days makes another Tool album particularly compelling because I want to continue exploring that atmosphere and rhythmic complexity.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being my next choice: The Blessed Hellride and Dirt appeal to me, but today I am more drawn to Tool and Master of Puppets."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy rock and metal, but sometimes miss why atmosphere, intricate riffs, and complex rhythms make certain albums stronger choices today."
}
